Author: Jagan Mohan R <dr@jm.gl>
Date:   Sat Apr 11 22:56:57 2026 +0530

    fix: jQuery.ui scope issue — shim re-exposes H5P.jQuery as global
    
    H5P core calls jQuery.noConflict(true), hiding jQuery from global scope.
    jQuery.ui's UMD wrapper then can't find jQuery and fails silently,
    leaving .tooltip(), .draggable(), .sortable() unattached. The 2-line
    shim before jQuery.ui restores window.jQuery = H5P.jQuery so jQuery.ui
    attaches its methods to the correct instance.
    
    Fixes ImageSequencing, DragText, and DragQuestion content types.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

